---
/**
 * Medicare Supplement (Medigap).
 *
 * The one page on the site with NO self-enrol button. Medigap underwriting,
 * state rules and the timing of your open enrolment are exactly the things a
 * form gets wrong, so the only action here is a conversation. That is a
 * deliberate difference from the Advantage page, not an oversight.
 *
 * The testimonials block is a clearly-labelled TEMPLATE. The entries are
 * obviously-fake samples, not attributed to anyone, and the banner above them
 * says so — a placeholder quote with a real-sounding name attached is a
 * fabricated endorsement, which is exactly what must not ship.
 */
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/CtaBand.astro';
import CompareMaMedigap from '../../components/CompareMaMedigap.astro';
import MedigapChart from '../../components/MedigapChart.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'Medicare Supplement (Medigap) Plans Explained | Lisa’s Insurance Agency';
const description =
  'What a Medicare Supplement covers, how the standardized plans A through N compare, how Medigap differs from Medicare Advantage, and why you still need Part D.';

/**
 * TEMPLATE ONLY. Placeholder structure so Lisa can see the shape of the block.
 * Not real people, not real quotes, not attributed. Replace wholesale with
 * sourced, verbatim reviews — do not edit these into "realistic" ones.
 */
const testimonialTemplate = [
  {
    quote: '[Client’s own words about what the process felt like — sourced review goes here.]',
    who: '[First name, state]',
  },
  {
    quote: '[Client’s own words about the service after enrolling — sourced review goes here.]',
    who: '[First name, state]',
  },
  {
    quote: '[Client’s own words about how a question got handled — sourced review goes here.]',
    who: '[First name, state]',
  },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is a Plan G from one company different from a Plan G from another?',
    a: 'Not in what it covers. The benefits under each plan letter are set by federal law, so every Plan G covers the same things. What differs between companies is the price, how they raise prices over time, and what they’re like to deal with when you need something.',
  },
  {
    q: 'When should I buy one?',
    a: 'Your Medigap open enrollment period starts the month you’re 65 or older and enrolled in Part B, and it runs six months. During it, you can buy any Medigap policy sold in your state regardless of your health. That protection is the reason timing matters so much here.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What if I apply after that window?',
    a: 'Outside of your open enrollment period and outside certain guaranteed-issue situations, companies may ask health questions and can decline your application or charge more based on the answers. The rules vary by state. If you’re past your enrollment window, call me before you apply anywhere.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does a Medigap policy cover my spouse too?',
    a: 'No. Medigap policies cover one person. If you and your spouse both want coverage, that’s two policies.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I keep it if I move to another state?',
    a: 'Generally Yes. Medigap isn’t network-based, so it travels with you. Tell me when you move anyway, because pricing and available plans can differ, and it’s worth a look.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it cost extra to buy through you?',
    a: 'No. The premium for a given policy is the same whether you go direct or through me. What you get by going through me is someone who compares the companies with you and stays reachable afterwards.',
  },
];
---

<Page
  title={title}
  description={description}
  rawTitle
  eyebrow="Medicare · Medigap"
  heading="Medicare Supplement (Medigap)"
  intro="Medicare Supplement (Medigap) plans work alongside Original Medicare to help cover your share of costs. These plans are identified by letters, such as Plan G or Plan N. Each letter represents a standardized set of benefits established by the federal government, so the coverage for the same letter is the same no matter which insurance company offers it."
>
  <!-- ─── What Medigap is ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section" id="what-it-is" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/medicare">Medicare</a> / Medicare Supplement</p>
      <p class="eyebrow">How Medigap works</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="what-heading">It fills the gaps Original Medicare leaves.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Hence the nickname. Original Medicare pays most of a covered bill and
          leaves you the rest. Medigap is what pays that rest.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Under Original Medicare on its own you’re responsible for deductibles,
          copayments and coinsurance, and there is no yearly limit on how much that
          adds up to. A Medigap policy takes over some or all of that share,
          depending on which plan letter you choose.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>There’s no network.</strong> A Medigap policy works with any
          doctor or hospital in the country that accepts Medicare, with no
          referrals and nothing to check before you travel. For people who split
          their year between two states, or who want to keep a specialist they’ve
          seen for years, that’s usually the deciding factor.
        </p>
        <p>
          It does one job and only that job. Prescriptions aren’t included — you
          add a separate Part D plan — and neither are routine dental, vision or
          hearing care.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="chips">
        <span class="chip">
          <svg class="mark" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M9 16.2 4.8 12l-1.4 1.4L9 19 21 7l-1.4-1.4z"/>
          </svg>
          Any doctor who accepts Medicare
        </span>
        <span class="chip">
          <svg class="mark" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M9 16.2 4.8 12l-1.4 1.4L9 19 21 7l-1.4-1.4z"/>
          </svg>
          No referrals, no network to check
        </span>
        <span class="chip">
          <svg class="mark" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M9 16.2 4.8 12l-1.4 1.4L9 19 21 7l-1.4-1.4z"/>
          </svg>
          Benefits set by law, identical across companies
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── Compare ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section--navy" id="compare" aria-labelledby="compare-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Compare</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="compare-heading">
          How does a Supplement compare to Medicare Advantage?
        </h2>
        <p class="lead">
          The two plans side by side. You choose one or the other. You can’t have
          both at once.
        </p>
      </div>

      <CompareMaMedigap stay="supplement" id="compare-heading" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── The lettered plans ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section" id="plans" aria-labelledby="plans-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The standardized plans</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="plans-heading">A through N, and what each one covers.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Medigap plans are standardized by law. Once you know which letter you
          want, the only remaining question is which company to buy it from.
        </p>
      </div>

      <MedigapChart />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── Why Part D ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section--navy" id="part-d" aria-labelledby="part-d-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Don’t skip this</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="part-d-heading">Why you still need Part D.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          A Medigap policy does not cover prescriptions. That’s not a gap in your
          plan; it’s a separate plan you need to add.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          People who take few or no regular medications often decide to skip Part D
          because it seems unnecessary. The concern is the late enrollment penalty.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you go without creditable prescription coverage after becoming
          eligible for Part D, enrolling later can trigger a penalty added to your
          premium. It’s not a one-time penalty charge. It can last as long as you
          have Part D and grow the longer you go without coverage.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you have drug coverage from somewhere else (an employer, a union, or
          the VA), it may count as creditable, in which case there’s no penalty for
          delaying. Whether yours counts is worth confirming rather than assuming.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="actions actions--stack">
        <a class="btn btn--accent" href="/medicare/prescription-drugs">
          Read about Part D
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={site.phoneHref}>Verify Coverage</a>
      </div>
      <p class="microline">Calling connects you with Lisa, a licensed insurance agent.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── Testimonials TEMPLATE ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section" id="testimonials" aria-labelledby="testimonials-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Client stories</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="testimonials-heading">What working together is like.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="callout callout--note">
        <h3>Template — not real reviews</h3>
        <p>
          The three cards below are an empty layout showing where sourced client
          reviews will sit. They are not quotes from real people and are not
          attributed to anyone. They get replaced wholesale with verbatim reviews
          once those are collected, with the client’s permission.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="cards cards--3" style="margin-top: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 44px)">
        {testimonialTemplate.map((item) => (
          <article class="card review-card">
            <p class="stars" aria-hidden="true">★★★★★</p>
            <blockquote>{item.quote}</blockquote>
            <footer>{item.who}</footer>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="reviews-footnote">
        Reviews will be shown exactly as written, and only with permission.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── How Lisa works ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section--navy" id="how-i-help" aria-labelledby="help-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">How I help</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="help-heading">Medigap is a phone call, not a checkout.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          There’s no enroll online button on this page on purpose. Timing, state
          rules, and health questions all decide what you can actually get, and a
          form can’t tell you that.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I’m an independent broker who works with multiple insurance companies.
          I’ll help you compare the options available to you, explain the
          differences, and point out when a change may not actually improve your
          situation.
        </p>
        <p>
          My role is to help people compare Medicare Supplement plan options from
          highly rated insurance companies. Ratings reflect financial strength and
          ability to pay claims, not price, service, or policy guarantees.
        </p>
        <p>
          After you enroll, I stay your agent. If you have any concerns regarding a
          rate change you don’t understand or a move to another state, call me.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="actions actions--stack">
        <a class="btn btn--accent" href={site.phoneHref}>Talk to Lisa · {site.phone}</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={site.smsHref}>Text me</a>
      </div>
      <p class="microline">Calling connects you with Lisa, a licensed insurance agent.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── FAQ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="faq-heading">Questions about Supplement plans.</h2>
      </div>

      <Faq items={faqs} schema />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Finding the Right Plan and Company"
    copy="That’s a fifteen-minute conversation, and it’s the one that saves people the most. No cost, no obligation, and no pressure to decide on the call."
  />
</Page>
